 To write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm using minimal memory and with error avoidance, follow the steps below:

First, let's create a simple bubble sort function:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

void bubbleSort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    size_t n = arr.size();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {
        for (size_t j = 0; j < n - i - 1; ++j) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

