 Certainly! Here's a PHP function called `smart_sort_array` that meets your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') { // Set default order to ascending
    $size = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $size - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $size - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order === 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order === 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function takes an associative array named `$set` as its first argument, and an optional second argument `$order` with two possible values: 'ASC' for ascending order or 'DESC' for descending order. By default, the order will be set to ascending.

