 Here's an R function named `check_numeric` that takes a character vector as input and returns a logical value indicating whether all non-NA elements in the vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
check_numeric <- function(char_vector) {
  not_na <- !is.na(char_vector)
  numeric_elements <- sapply(char_vector[not_na], function(x) {
    tryCatch(as.numeric(x), error = function(e) NA) != NA
  })
  all(numeric_elements)
}

# Helper function for higher verbosity
convert_to_numeric <- function(x) {
  tryCatch(as.numeric(x), error = function(e) NA)
}

# Test case
test_vector <- c("1", "2.5", "three", NA, "4", "five")
print(check_numeric(test_vector))
```

